 abstract = {The existence, properties, and dynamics of the dark sectors of our universe pose fundamental challenges to our current model of physics, and large-scale astronomical surveys may be our only hope to unravel these long-standing mysteries. In this white paper, we describe the science motivation, instrumentation, and survey plan for the next-generation spectroscopic observatory, the Stage-5 Spectroscopic Experiment (Spec-S5). Spec-S5 is a new all-sky spectroscopic instrument optimized to efficiently carry out cosmological surveys of unprecedented scale and precision. The baseline plan for Spec-S5 involves upgrading two existing 4-m telescopes to new 6-m wide-field facilities, each with a highly multiplexed spectroscopic instrument capable of simultaneously measuring the spectra of 13,000 astronomical targets. Spec-S5, which builds and improves on the hardware used for previous cosmology experiments, represents a cost-effective and rapid approach to realizing a more than 10 gain in spectroscopic capability compared to the current state-of-the-art represented by the Dark Energy Spectroscopic Instrument project (DESI). Spec-S5 will provide a critical scientific capability in the post-Rubin and post-DESI era for advancing cosmology, fundamental physics, and astrophysics in the 2030s.},
 author = {Robert Besuner and Dustin A Lang and G Tarlé and LM Schmidt and Biprateep Dey and David Kirkby and Vera Gluscevic and Nicholas R Wenner and Eva Silverstein and Etienne Burtin and Stephen Bailey and John Moustakas and Kyle S Dawson and Timothy Fanning and Gaston Gutierrez and David J Schlegel and Matthew Lewandowski and Chris Stone and Joan Najita and Anand Raichoor and Kenneth W Lin and Emanuele Castorina and Robert Stupak and Jeff Newman and Guillermo Fernandez Moroni and Stephen Heathcote and Rongpu Zhou and Michael Schubnell and Priscila Pires and Martin White and Joshua A Frieman and Stephanie Escoffier and Constance M Rockosi and Klaus Honscheid and Andreu Font-Ribera and Armin Karcher and Steve Holland and Jaime E Forero-Romero and Alexie Leauthaud and Alex Drlica-Wagner and F Chierchie and Jennifer L Marshall and Olivier Doré and Daniel Green and Richard Joyce and Abby Bault and Ofer Lahav and Luke MG Tyas and Sailer Noah and Zachary Slepian and Konstantina Boutsia and M Vargas-Magaña and Stephen Kent and Eric Jullo and Timothy Abbot and Alex Krolewski and Santiago Avila and Haruki Ebina and Patrick McDonald and Steve Heathcote and Stephen E Holland and Swayamtrupta Panda and Adam Myers and Satya Gontcho A Gontcho and Nathalie Palanque-Delabrouile and Malak Galal and Eusebio Sanchez and Claire Juramy and Stéphanie Juneau and Blas Irigoyen Gimenez and Paul Martini and Juan Estrada and Maxime Rombach and AJ Lapi and Parker Fagrelius and Moritz Münchmeyer and Ashley Ross and Joseph H Silber and Claire L Poppett and Jeffrey A Newman and Timothy N Miller and Kevan Hashemi and Kevin Fanning and Rebekah A Sebok and Jean-Paul Kneib and Patrick Dunlop and Patrick Jelinsky and Sean MacBride and Julien Guy and Ting S Li and Roberto Avilés and William Coulton and Mohamed Bouri and Yuanyuan Zhang and Christophe Magneville and Oliver HE Philcox and Christophe Yèche and Simone Ferraro and Alistair Walker and Mikhail M Ivanov and Lori E Allen and Elisabeth Krause 